      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(voice-call): handle spawn error on tailscale stop cleanup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nstopTailscaleTunnel spawns tailscale without an error handler. Missing binary (ENOENT) causes an unhandled error crash AND the promise hangs forever.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd proc.on(\"error\", handler) that cleans up the timeout and resolves the promise. Same pattern already used for ngrok spawns at lines 154 and 200 in the same file.\n\n## User Impact\n\nVoice-call tunnel cleanup no longer crashes or hangs when tailscale is missing.\n\n## Evidence\n\nLive proof: exact reproduction of production stopTailscaleTunnel function with nonexistent binary. Error handler catches the error and resolves the promise. Process survives.\n\nRegression test (10 passed).\n\n## Risk\n\nLow. One-line handler matching existing patterns in the same file.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
